{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: Three completed experiments show RNA-only (0.485) and two multimodal variants with ResNet50 (0.527 concat, 0.523 weighted), confirming that adding an image modality improves performance by ~4%. However, we have no image-only baseline, so we cannot decompose whether the multimodal gain comes from complementary information or simply from the image modality being strong on its own. Question tested: config_010 (image-only, single profile, ResNet50) isolates the image contribution. If image-only performs near 0.52, the RNA signal adds little and future effort should focus on image encoders; if it performs much lower (~0.35-0.40), the gain is truly synergistic and fusion strategy becomes critical. Why best next experiment: With only 3 data points, the evidence is sparse and the most important design uncertainty is the independent contribution of each modality. Resolving this single question reframes the entire remaining search (which encoder to improve, whether fusion matters, whether multi-profile aggregation is needed) and prevents misallocating limited budget on the wrong axis."
}

